{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112395","id":2978339538,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6xhdrS","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112395","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112395.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112395.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112395","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112395/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112395/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112395/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f28af3d5535d0d8a610baeda9dbc7a529a8b70f5","number":112395,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add `float` overloads to `Randfn` and `RandRange` methods in C#","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This issue aims to implement a small part of https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12356 in making random number generation more consistent/complete in C#.\r\n\r\nHere are the main changes:\r\n- Add `float GD.Randfn(float, float)` to match `double GD.Randfn(double, double)`\r\n- Add `float GD.RandRange(float, float)` to match `double GD.RandRange(double, double)`\r\n- Documentation comment fixes\r\n\r\nFull list of changes:\r\n- Add `float GD.Randfn(float, float)`:\r\n  - Add `float Math::randfn(float, float)` to match `double Math::randfn(double, double)`\r\n  - Add `float godotsharp_randfn32(float, float)` to match `double godotsharp_randfn(double, double)`\r\n  - Fix a documentation comment error in `double Randfn(double, double)`\r\n- Add `float GD.RandRange(float, float)`:\r\n  - Add `float godotsharp_randf32_range(float, float)` to match `double godotsharp_randf_range(double, double)`\r\n- Fix two documentation comment errors in `uint GD.RandFromSeed(ref ulong)`\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I wasn't able to implement most of what I suggested in the proposal because of the following issues:\r\n- There is no way to generate a 64-bit integer in Godot core due to the use of `pcg32_random_t` rather than `pcg64_random_t`.\r\n- There is no way to have multiple overloads in GDExtension, therefore I couldn't add `double RandomNumberGenerator.Randfn(double, double)`. I also couldn't add a method with a new name for this because the original uses `real_t` rather than `float`/`double`.\r\n- I didn't want to change the return type of `long RandomNumberGenerator.RandWeighted(float[])` because it's a binary-breaking change, and also it's based on the C++ implementation which uses 64-bit indexes for vectors.\r\n\r\nNevertheless, I think this a good start, since `float` is widely used in Godot C#. In my own projects, I have to write code like `(float)GD.RandRange(0f, 1f)`.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","descri